
////////////////INTRO//////////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_frodo107
"Frodo: Bilbo once told me... his part in this tale would end... that each of us must come and go in the telling"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_frodo108
"Frodo: Bilbo's story was now over... there would be no more journeys for him... save one."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_bilbo005
"Bilbo: Tell me again lad... where are we going?"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_frodo109
"Frodo: To the harbour Bilbo... the elves have accorded you a special honour...\n a place on the last ship to leave Middle-Earth."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gandalf428
"Gandalf: Once you are ready, my dear Bilbo, come and see me at the dock. \n But do not be too hasty, for this is an adventure that neither you nor I shall return from."
END


////////////////GIL GALAD//////////////////

SCRIPT:mgfotr_pippin152
"Ereinion Gil-galad; Last High King of the Noldor."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_sam188
"Gil-galad was an elven-king.\n Of him the harpers sadly sing;"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_sam189
"the last whose realm was fair and free,\n between the Mountains and the Sea."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_sam190
"His sword was long, his lance was keen.\n His shining helm afar was seen;"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_sam191
"the countless stars of heaven's field,\n were mirrored in his silver shield."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_sam192
"But long ago he rode away,\n and where he dwelleth none can say;"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_sam193
"for into darkness fell his star,\n in Mordor where the shadows are."
END



////////////////GILDOR//////////////////


SCRIPT:mgfotr_gildor013
"It brightens my spirit to see you, Frodo. Word of your bravery and sacrifice has reached far.\n I hope the end of your journey will bring you peace."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_frodo112
"Your aid proved invaluable, Gildor Inglorion. Middle-earth owes you a great debt."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_gildor014
"Think nothing of it, my friends. May the light of Telperion ever illuminate your paths."
END


////////////////STONE//////////////////


SCRIPT:mgfotr_sam174
"What does it say, mister Frodo?"
END


SCRIPT:mgfotr_frodo137
"It is a stone commemorating the first arrival of the Men of Westernesse in Middle-earth, in the year 600 of the Second Age."
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_frodo138
"Veantur was their captain's name. Their ship was Entulesse."
END

////////////////CIRCLE//////////////////
SCRIPT:mgfotr_bilbo012
"My what a beautiful place"
END

SCRIPT:mgfotr_bilbo015
"Look at that tree... how old do you think it is?"
END

